        "Day": "02"
      },
      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {
        "CopyrightInformation": "Copyright © 2016 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.",
        "AbstractText": [
          {
            "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
            "Label": "STUDY OBJECTIVE",
            "content": "We hypothesized that oral administration of a single dose of pregabalin 2 hours before modified radical mastectomy (MRM) would produce dose-related reduction in postoperative opioid consumption."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "DESIGN",
            "content": "Prospective randomized controlled clinical trial."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "SETTING",
            "content": "Postanesthesia care unit."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "PATIENTS",
            "content": "One hundred twenty adult women scheduled for unilateral (MRM) with axillary evacuation."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "INTERVENTIONS",
            "content": "Patients were randomized to receive either, placebo capsule, pregabalin 75 mg, pregabalin 150 mg, or pregabalin 300 mg."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
            "Label": "MEASUREMENTS",
            "content": "The assessment parameters were the postoperative analgesic effect using visual analog scale (VAS) pain scores, the subsequent 24-hour morphine consumption, and the systemic adverse effects of pregabalin doses."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
            "Label": "MAIN RESULTS",
            "content": "The VAS score at rest and movement was significantly decreased only in group P300 and group P150 in comparison to group P0 and group P75 at 0 hour (P<.01). The median (interquartile range) consumption of morphine in the first postoperative 24 hours was significantly decreased in group P300 in comparison to group P0 and group P75 (P300 vs P0: 6.5 [5-6.5] vs 20.5 [15.8-20.5] [P<.001]; P300 vs P75: 6.5 [5-6.5] vs 20 [14-20] [P<.001]), but there was no significant difference between group P300 and group P150. In addition, there was a significant decrease in consumption of morphine in group P150 in comparison to group P0 and group P75 (P150 vs P0: 7 [5-7] vs 20.5 [15.8-20.5] [P<.001]; P150 vs P75: 7 [5-7] vs 20 [14-20] [P<.001]). There were statistical significant increase in dizziness and blurred vision in group P300 in comparison to other groups (P<.05)."
          },
          {
            "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "Label": "CONCLUSIONS",
            "content": "A single preoperative oral dose of pregabalin 150 mg is an optimal dose for reducing postoperative pain and morphine consumption in patients undergoing MRM."
          }
        ]
      },
